yoagent's stdio spawn takes only an additive env map (cmd.env(k, v)): it has no env_remove and no env_clear. So yoyo can't unset an inherited key through that API. Posting the comment:
  ╭─ Turn 30 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  ▶ $ cd /home/runner/work/yoyo-evolve/yoyo-evolve; cat > /tmp/c.m… (13 lines) ✓ (895ms)

Shell hooks no longer get your provider API keys by default. Set YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0 (or false) to turn that off. Committed as 0d6f8985 (titled "Part of #1064", not "Fixes"). Build, the full test suite (--no-fail-fast), clippy and fmt all pass.

Where hooks start: git grep finds exactly one place a hook process is started: ShellHook::run_command in src/hooks.rs:741. Its only callers are the three hook phases (before a tool runs, after it runs, after it fails). All three now pass the list of key variables to remove. That list is re-read from the environment every time a hook starts, and the removal happens after the hook's own TOOL_* variables are set.

How the setting is read:
• Hooks: keys are removed when the variable is unset, 1 or true. Only 0 or false (any case, spaces trimmed) keeps them. An empty value or a typo still removes them, so a mistyped opt-out stays safe.
• The model's bash, `/run`, `!`, `/bg`, `/watch`: unchanged. They only remove keys when you set 1 or true. One table test checks both rules for each value.
• apply_scrub_std is new: the hook code uses the synchronous std::process::Command, and the existing helper only handled tokio's.

Tests: three spawn tests in src/hooks_scrub_tests.rs run a real hook. They set the API key and an ordinary variable on the hook's own command, never on yoyo's process. The key is gone by default and with 1, and still there with 0 or false. The ordinary variable arrives in every case. The tests sit in their own file because hooks.rs is already over its line limit.

As a check, I temporarily made the unset case not remove keys, in one mutate→test→restore command. Exactly the default-case spawn test and the table test failed. I restored the code and no "NEUTERED" marker is left.

Docs: docs/src/troubleshooting/safety.md now gives the default for each kind of program and how to opt out, and lists what isn't covered yet. There's also a new Day 238 entry in ARCHITECTURE.md.

What's left, posted on #1064:
• MCP stdio servers: yoyo can't unset an inherited key through yoagent 0.25.13's stdio launcher. Its env argument can only add variables, so nothing there removes or clears one. The options I see are an upstream request, setting each key to "" (which isn't the same as unset), or wrapping the command in env -u (Unix only). I haven't picked one.
• `/run`, `!`, `/bg`, `/watch`: these should honour YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=1 as an opt-in, but don't yet.
• `.yoyo/goal_verify.md`: its command (run_verify_command in src/commands_goal.rs) is also written by the repository and still gets your keys. It isn't a hook, so it was outside this slice.
